{
  "method": "Residential land = districts where Table 2-2 allows at least one building type whose 'Number of Principal Units' row admits a dwelling. Family status per district: a building type allowed in the zone (Table 2-2 check mark) admits a k-unit building when its unit rule permits k units: 'No limits' = 1 or more, 'N max.' = 1 to N, '3 min.'/'3 minimum' = 3 or more, '1 in House' = exactly 1, '2 with special permit' = 2 only after a hearing (hearing status). A Double House A has at least 2 units (Sec. 3.80.1: two House A types side by side). 4+-family means a building type that can hold 4 or more units. Storefront/Commercial House dwelling entries marked '8' (upper stories only) are counted as allowed. The backyard-cottage unit in NX1/NX2 is not counted toward the 4+ test (Row Building already allows 4+ there). Shares use our gross parcel acreage (data/land_area/bridgeport.json), not NZA's net of protected land.",
  "source": "public/sources/bridgeport-zoning.pdf (Zone Bridgeport, Table 2-2 and Sec. 3.20-3.120, 4.70, 8.20.1); data/land_area/bridgeport.json; NZA data in data/nza_replication/nza_snapshots.json and data/towns/bridgeport.json",
